  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Aces and Kings. Logic: Complete all eight foundations, four building up from ace to king and four building down from king to ace, without regard to suit.',
    Player: 'Aces and Kings is a difficult two-deck solitaire in which eight foundations build both upward from aces and downward from kings without regard to suit.',
    objective: 'Complete all eight foundations, four building up from ace to king and four building down from king to ace, without regard to suit.',
    gameplay: 'Cards from the tableau, reserve, waste, and compatible foundations may be moved to foundations. Tableau spaces are immediately refilled from the stock. When the stock is exhausted the deal ends, so every foundation transfer must preserve enough flexibility to finish.',
    keyRules: [
      'Eight foundations split between ascending and descending builds.',
      'Two thirteen-card reserves can only feed foundations.',
      'Empty tableau spaces are filled from stock immediately.',
      'Foundation-to-foundation transfers are allowed when ranks fit.',
    ],
